[[:db/retract 17592186117557 :answer-field/choices 17592186117558] [:db/retract 17592186117557 :answer-field/choices 17592186117559] [:db/retract 17592186117557 :answer-field/choices 17592186117560] [:db/retract 17592186117557 :answer-field/choices 17592186117561] [:db/retract 17592186117557 :answer-field/choices 17592186117562] {:db/id 17592186120233 :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(0,2,1)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$\\frac{x-1}{-2}=\\frac{y-3}{1}=\\frac{z}{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,2,1⟩.$ From the canonical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨-2,1,5⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨-2,1,5⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,1,5⟩ & =⟨0,2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,1,5⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,1,5⟩ & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,1,5⟩ & =7 \\\\ -2x+y+5z & =7 \\\\ -2x+y+5z-7 & =0 \\\\ 2x-y-5z+7 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186117557 :answer-field/correct "answer-c2a52ec1-f084-5a8c-880c-5ed843166cc3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0395970e-0d9a-5762-bb5c-e46f2d38b8c0" "answer-c2a52ec1-f084-5a8c-880c-5ed843166cc3" "answer-a9e87eac-968b-5331-95b6-4aa94e8c328b" "answer-5e5c8545-4573-5ed8-bdbb-b47cb8a05b58" "answer-4b65c837-ece2-5b2d-a1d6-63cd8cc028b3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0395970e-0d9a-5762-bb5c-e46f2d38b8c0" :answer/id #uuid "0395970e-0d9a-5762-bb5c-e46f2d38b8c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-y-5z+11=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c2a52ec1-f084-5a8c-880c-5ed843166cc3" :answer/id #uuid "c2a52ec1-f084-5a8c-880c-5ed843166cc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-y-5z+7=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9e87eac-968b-5331-95b6-4aa94e8c328b" :answer/id #uuid "a9e87eac-968b-5331-95b6-4aa94e8c328b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2y+z+7=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e5c8545-4573-5ed8-bdbb-b47cb8a05b58" :answer/id #uuid "5e5c8545-4573-5ed8-bdbb-b47cb8a05b58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+3y-1=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b65c837-ece2-5b2d-a1d6-63cd8cc028b3" :answer/id #uuid "4b65c837-ece2-5b2d-a1d6-63cd8cc028b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+3y-7=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119834 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e005b4ab-002a-57d1-b9b7-3fc85eeb395f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e005b4ab-002a-57d1-b9b7-3fc85eeb395f" :question/id #uuid "e005b4ab-002a-57d1-b9b7-3fc85eeb395f" :question/math-academy-id "q-70819" :question/problem "Given the Cartesian equation $x-2y+3z=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨1,-2,3⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-2y+3z & =0 \\\\ 3z & =-x+2y \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{2}{3}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $x=0$ and $y=0$, we get $z=0.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,0)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,0⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,-2,3⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0fa9de33-9d04-55cd-94a1-cecb483c4e8f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0fa9de33-9d04-55cd-94a1-cecb483c4e8f" :answer-field/id #uuid "0fa9de33-9d04-55cd-94a1-cecb483c4e8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-95f99c20-a235-5660-8d6b-b04b727483d7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-95f99c20-a235-5660-8d6b-b04b727483d7" "answer-1d1ce09d-4b43-5ecf-b718-dbc33ca70dc2" "answer-13bd6234-56f6-541c-bfc5-f390a8cb5bfa" "answer-2c57426d-3447-5790-bc09-7f27391e4e89" "answer-b1292071-77e9-579a-8b2f-0a1e4da37f19"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95f99c20-a235-5660-8d6b-b04b727483d7" :answer/id #uuid "95f99c20-a235-5660-8d6b-b04b727483d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,-2,3⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d1ce09d-4b43-5ecf-b718-dbc33ca70dc2" :answer/id #uuid "1d1ce09d-4b43-5ecf-b718-dbc33ca70dc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,2,3⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13bd6234-56f6-541c-bfc5-f390a8cb5bfa" :answer/id #uuid "13bd6234-56f6-541c-bfc5-f390a8cb5bfa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨3,-2,1⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c57426d-3447-5790-bc09-7f27391e4e89" :answer/id #uuid "2c57426d-3447-5790-bc09-7f27391e4e89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,3⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,-2,3⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1292071-77e9-579a-8b2f-0a1e4da37f19" :answer/id #uuid "b1292071-77e9-579a-8b2f-0a1e4da37f19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,\\frac{1}{3}⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,-2,3⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-2e339301-4273-5fe3-adcf-f9263b991a91" :activity/id #uuid "2e339301-4273-5fe3-adcf-f9263b991a91" :activity/title "The Cartesian Equation of a Plane" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050830 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-3d11e9af-f90d-5fbe-a96b-a527fdd70135" "step-eee37068-88fb-59e1-930d-db5693058840" "step-24b7f863-ce6a-5264-b6ec-ac8e65ecdb05"] :activity/first-step "step-3d11e9af-f90d-5fbe-a96b-a527fdd70135" :db/ensure [:activ